course: dictionary
lesson: 7246
title: Picnic: a noun, a verb, and an idiom
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A picnic is a meal eaten outside, often in a park or on a beach, sitting on a blanket. «The family packed a picnic basket with sandwiches and juice.» The word basket and the words sandwiches and juice are the clues: a picnic is food you carry outside to eat.
explain: Picnic can also be a verb, a doing word. To picnic means to have a picnic. «We will picnic by the lake on Sunday.» Ask yourself: does picnic name a thing, or describe an action? Here we will do something, so picnic is a verb.
explain: «No picnic» is an idiom, a phrase that does not mean what the words say. «Moving house is no picnic.» Moving house means boxes, heavy lifting and hard work, so no picnic means not easy. Always check the whole sentence, not just one word.
fact: A picnic is a meal eaten outside, often in a park or on a beach, sitting on a blanket.
fact: «Picnic» can be a noun or a verb: «We had a picnic» and «We picnic by the river».
fact: «No picnic» means not easy: «Moving house is no picnic».
fact: Good picnic habits: keep food cool, take your rubbish home, and watch out for wasps and the sun.
fact: Ants can ruin a picnic, so check the ground before you sit down.
exercise: «The family ate their lunch on a blanket in the park.» What is a picnic? | A race around a running track | A meal eaten in bed | *A meal eaten outside, often on a blanket | A kind of shop
exercise: «Moving house is no picnic.» What does no picnic mean? | Full of food | Very fun | Cold and wet | *Not easy
exercise: «We will picnic by the lake on Sunday.» What does picnic mean here? | *To have a picnic | A large meal indoors | To cook a dinner | To go swimming
test: «The family packed a picnic basket with sandwiches and juice.» What was in the basket? | Bricks and sand | Shoes and socks | Books and pencils | *Sandwiches and juice
test: Which is a good habit at a picnic? | Leave food in the sun all day | Feed the wasps | *Take your rubbish home | Leave rubbish on the grass
exam: Jayden says «Moving house is no picnic» means moving is fun. Who is right? | Both are wrong: it means cold | *Jayden is wrong: it means not easy | Jayden is right: it means fun | Neither: it is a meal
